+// The top of the sidebar when the address bar lives there. It borrows the
+// toolbar's own views (back, forward, reload, home, pinned actions, and the
+// location bar, plus the profile button and app menu for the footer) instead
+// of creating copies, so every bubble, shortcut, and element identifier keeps
+// working. The toolbar itself is hidden while the views are borrowed. They go
+// back when the setting is off, the layout changes, or the window closes.
+// Extensions stay in the hidden toolbar; the site controls list them.
+//
+// The header is only shown while the sidebar is full. The footer shows in
+// every sidebar state.
+//
